From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:07:43 -0500
Subject: fix: an empty Space shows its page; pinned folders collapse; the
 sidebar field's icons come back (S-408, S-409, S-410, S-412, S-413)

An empty Space (tabs R66; spaces B3, B4, B20): a switch to a Space with no
tab, the close of a Space's last row and a Clear that leaves nothing opened
a New Tab there, a row the Space had not asked for. They now show the
Space's own page, the stand-in a sleep shows since beta 8, which the
sidebar does not list. A switch from it to another empty Space keeps it for
that Space, closing it opens another, and Clear leaves it alone. A tab that
leaves for another window, mid-drag, still leaves a New Tab behind it.

The New Tab page's bookmarks bar (new-tab N9): "Show tab groups" is off at
first. The profile saves every tab group, one an extension makes around a
tab it drives included, and its chip with the tab groups button showed on
the New Tab page of every Space; with no bookmarks it alone brought the bar
out. The sidebar lists a window's groups in their Space.

Folders F3 (GitHub issue 76): a collapsed folder kept every awake pin of
the Space listed, so a pinned folder whose pins were all awake seemed never
to collapse. A collapse now folds every row but the one on screen; a pin
the user leaves while the folder is collapsed stays listed while awake
(issue 35), until the folder is opened.

The sidebar's address field (sidebar Y49; GitHub issue 45): the field
offered the extensions' row only the width it had, and the row sizes itself
to what it is offered, so pinned icons once folded into the menu never came
back while animations were on. It is offered the field's room less the
site's name's minimum.

Install as an app (site-controls Si14): Chromium's Install chip and icon
are gone from the toolbar's address field as from the sidebar's, with the
prompt that points at them; the site panel's row installs the page.

Settings (T3, T46; GitHub issue 74): the little-window row says first that
a link from another app opens in a window of its own whatever the peek
settings say, and "Show a peek" that it is for a link from a pinned tab.

Why: the owner, 2026-11-04 (a screenshot of an empty Space beside an
extension's tab group; the Install chip), and GitHub issues 45, 74 and 76.
Removable when: never as behaviour.
